WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.769
- Hello, I'm Gav.
- I'm Dan.

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:04.504
Welcome to
the "The Super Slow Show."

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:07.640
You've joined us here
on a nice, sunny day
at our pool.

00:00:07.673 --> 00:00:08.708
- Lovely, isn't it?
- Lovely.

00:00:08.741 --> 00:00:10.276
We're just relaxing

00:00:10.309 --> 00:00:11.744
because we've been told
our special guest

00:00:11.777 --> 00:00:13.646
is definitely
going to be late,

00:00:13.679 --> 00:00:16.149
but is also definitely arriving
in style, whatever that means.

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:17.617
- That's what I've heard.
- Yeah.

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:20.553
- ( motorcycle rumbling )
- You hear something?

00:00:20.586 --> 00:00:22.188
- Ahh. What is that?
- Something in the distance?

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:41.207
- He did arrive in style.
- He did.

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:44.477
That's what it means.
Fair play.

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:47.313
( theme music playing )

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:55.421
Dan: He's doing a wheelie,
for goodness sake.

00:00:55.454 --> 00:00:57.657
As if the entrance
wasn't good enough,

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.592
you had to wheelie
up to us.

00:00:59.625 --> 00:01:03.262
Well, I figured since
you guys gave me such
a sweet neck brace here

00:01:03.295 --> 00:01:04.697
on "The Super Slow Show,"

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:07.233
that I should give you guys
a little wheelie show.

00:01:07.266 --> 00:01:10.269
Gav: This is Andy Bell,
who just jumped over our pool

00:01:10.302 --> 00:01:12.839
with a Phantom on his head,
which isn't light.

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:14.440
It's a Phantom Miro.

00:01:14.473 --> 00:01:15.842
It's a smaller one
than what we usually use,

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:17.743
but it's still--
it's not small.

00:01:17.776 --> 00:01:20.847
I thought helmet-camera
technology was getting
better these days.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:24.183
This is, like, about a 25-pound
dumbbell on my head.

00:01:24.216 --> 00:01:25.718
I have to say that was
the best entrance I've seen

00:01:25.751 --> 00:01:28.354
to a Slow Mo Guys video,
and I'm very jealous.

00:01:28.387 --> 00:01:29.789
You know,
I wish I could do that.

00:01:29.822 --> 00:01:31.791
If you did this better
than you did skateboarding,

00:01:31.824 --> 00:01:34.193
you would be fine.

00:01:34.226 --> 00:01:38.397
So, apparently, you're going
to do a pretty sweet stunt
on this pool.

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:40.600
Would you like to describe
the stunt for us?

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:43.402
"Apparently," um...

00:01:43.435 --> 00:01:45.471
This is where things
get kind of sketchy.

00:01:45.504 --> 00:01:47.340
Um, we have a pool.

00:01:47.373 --> 00:01:48.741
It's not that big,

00:01:48.774 --> 00:01:51.444
so we're going to go
corner to corner.

00:01:51.477 --> 00:01:54.714
Skimming a pool has only been
done a couple time successfully.

00:01:54.747 --> 00:01:58.317
Wait. So you're going to ride
the bike across the pool.

00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:01.921
The plan is to ride
the bike across the pool.

00:02:01.954 --> 00:02:04.624
You're going to try and ride
the bike across the pool.

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:06.292
I'm going to try and ride
the bike across the pool.

00:02:06.325 --> 00:02:08.828
Supposedly--
I'm no mathematician--

00:02:08.861 --> 00:02:11.430
but supposedly there's something
called surface tension

00:02:11.463 --> 00:02:13.166
that will keep me afloat

00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:14.700
if I'm going fast enough.

00:02:14.733 --> 00:02:18.771
Problem is is I don't know
how fast "fast enough" is.

00:02:18.804 --> 00:02:20.573
You guys have lab coats.
Can you tell me?

00:02:20.606 --> 00:02:23.910
- Um, I'll tell you what.
- This one's just for show.

00:02:23.943 --> 00:02:26.512
As fast as you can go,
I guess.

00:02:26.545 --> 00:02:27.880
All right, we'll get
out of your hair,

00:02:27.913 --> 00:02:30.249
set up some cameras,
and then it's all you.

00:02:30.282 --> 00:02:32.451
So I was going to say Andy's
about to defy physics,

00:02:32.484 --> 00:02:34.353
but really he's just going
to prove physics right now.

00:02:34.386 --> 00:02:35.855
Dan: I'm psyching myself
up for him.

00:02:35.888 --> 00:02:37.690
- I'm nervous for him.
- Gav: I'm nervous, too.

00:02:37.723 --> 00:02:39.759
- Go on.
- He's got the speed.

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:41.360
Go on.

00:02:41.393 --> 00:02:43.296
- Go on!
- He is bookin' it.

00:02:43.329 --> 00:02:45.798
Dan:
You got this!
You got this!

00:02:45.831 --> 00:02:46.966
( together )
Yeah!

00:02:46.999 --> 00:02:48.834
- He did it.
- Yeah!

00:02:48.867 --> 00:02:50.670
- Like it was nothing.
- Nailed it.

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:53.406
He just did it
like it was nothing.

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:55.275
Celebratory wheelie.

00:02:56.508 --> 00:02:58.377
Oh!

00:02:58.410 --> 00:03:00.546
You did it.
Congrats.

00:03:00.579 --> 00:03:03.482
- Oh, that is so scary.
- ( both laugh )

00:03:03.515 --> 00:03:04.617
All that buildup?

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:05.918
All that buildup
and it's done.

00:03:05.951 --> 00:03:07.787
Like it was nothing.

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:09.689
I bet the buildup was worse
than actually doing it, right?

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:11.891
- Yeah.
- You just went straight
 across there.

00:03:11.924 --> 00:03:13.859
Surface tension,
lab coat guy.

00:03:13.892 --> 00:03:16.495
Yeah, you just proved physics.

00:03:16.528 --> 00:03:17.897
I knew that would happen.
Yeah.

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:19.398
Yeah, you knew.
You told me.

00:03:19.431 --> 00:03:21.334
You told me to go that speed,
too. Thank you.

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:23.903
Would you like
to see that back
in wonderful slow motion?

00:03:23.936 --> 00:03:26.639
Um, yeah, let's take a look
and see what happened.

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:29.709
Ahh.
Nice A.C.

00:03:29.742 --> 00:03:31.777
Oh, it's nice in here.

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:34.780
- ( grunts ) Don't wanna crash.
- ( metal clatters )

00:03:34.813 --> 00:03:37.450
Don't worry about it.
Typical. It's a cheap table.

00:03:39.518 --> 00:03:42.021
Dan:  Even the pelican's,
 like, watching you.

00:03:42.054 --> 00:03:44.490
-  He just cocked his head. 
-  He's like, "What's gonna
 happen here?"

00:03:44.523 --> 00:03:45.791
"Pelican"? It's a flamingo.

00:03:45.824 --> 00:03:47.460
Oh, flamingo, whatever.

00:03:49.895 --> 00:03:51.497
- Dan:  Look at that. 
- Andy:  Whoa!

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:52.932
Dan:  It looks like
 it's the road.

00:03:52.965 --> 00:03:55.534
Guess you can ride on water.

00:03:55.567 --> 00:03:58.671
With hair like that you can.

00:03:58.704 --> 00:04:01.374
Andy:  Well, it looks
like the back tire
actually went deeper

00:04:01.407 --> 00:04:02.842
and then came up.

00:04:15.688 --> 00:04:17.823
Gav:  It's really cool
 because the individual
 grips on the tires

00:04:17.856 --> 00:04:19.692
separates out
 the water with the air,

00:04:19.725 --> 00:04:21.994
and then your foot,
like, kicks it at the back--

00:04:22.027 --> 00:04:23.996
- Andy:
Oh, and then spreads it-- 
- Gav:  And spreads it out more.

00:04:24.029 --> 00:04:27.633
Andy:  Yeah you can see
how far I got kicked.

00:04:27.666 --> 00:04:31.404
Gav:  You were on the ground,
 in the water,
 and then in the air

00:04:31.437 --> 00:04:34.373
within about one second.

00:04:34.406 --> 00:04:37.310
Wow, yeah. No wonder I was
having trouble braking,

00:04:37.343 --> 00:04:38.844
because I didn't even
get to hit the brakes

00:04:38.877 --> 00:04:40.880
about 60 feet
after the pool.

00:04:40.913 --> 00:04:43.082
Andy, that was insane.

00:04:43.115 --> 00:04:44.650
Classic footage.

00:04:44.683 --> 00:04:46.385
Gotta be the best thing
I've ever seen

00:04:46.418 --> 00:04:48.654
anyone do on this channel,
and I'm glad about it

00:04:48.687 --> 00:04:50.556
because I'm never going to be
able to do anything that good.

00:04:50.589 --> 00:04:52.625
That's a pretty big accolade.
Thank you.

00:04:52.658 --> 00:04:54.093
Dan:
 It was amazing.

00:04:54.126 --> 00:04:55.461
Gav:  That was some
 of the best-looking

00:04:55.494 --> 00:04:57.096
slow-mo footage I've ever seen.

00:04:57.129 --> 00:04:58.898
Andy:  Coming from you,
you've seen a little bit of it.

00:04:58.931 --> 00:05:00.733
-  Seen a lot, yeah. 
- Dan:  I was so pumped for you.

00:05:00.766 --> 00:05:02.601
I was just like,
"Come on, come on" all the way,

00:05:02.634 --> 00:05:03.869
on the way for you to actually
 do the stunt.

00:05:03.902 --> 00:05:05.104
Yeah, my heart was racing.

00:05:05.137 --> 00:05:06.439
I can't imagine
what yours was doing.

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:07.040
It was terrible.

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:10.480
You definitely deserve
a "Super Slow Show" lab coat,
Andy.

00:05:10.509 --> 00:05:12.078
Yeah!

00:05:12.111 --> 00:05:14.046
You can either wear it or
just clean your bike with it.

00:05:14.079 --> 00:05:16.015
This is awesome, guys.
Thank you so much.

00:05:16.048 --> 00:05:17.583
I feel like
I'm part of the team.

00:05:17.616 --> 00:05:18.851
I don't have the cool
British accent,

00:05:18.884 --> 00:05:20.553
but I got
a Canadian one, so...

00:05:20.586 --> 00:05:21.620
Absolutely part of the team.

00:05:21.653 --> 00:05:24.557
You risked this for us.

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:26.058
Yes, I did.

00:05:26.091 --> 00:05:28.561
Well, thanks very much
for lending us your guts.

00:05:28.594 --> 00:05:30.363
Thanks, guys.
Thank you so much.

00:05:30.396 --> 00:05:31.797
And thank you for watching.

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:33.666
Feel free to subscribe
to The Slow Mo Guys

00:05:33.699 --> 00:05:35.034
and we'll see you
in the next episode

00:05:35.067 --> 00:05:37.069
of "The Super Slow Show."

00:05:37.102 --> 00:05:39.739
Is there any reason why
I'm not wearing a shirt
at this point?

00:05:43.575 --> 00:05:44.844
Hello, the Internet.

00:05:44.877 --> 00:05:46.479
- Gav here.
- And Dan.

00:05:46.512 --> 00:05:48.013
If you didn't already,
please subscribe

00:05:48.046 --> 00:05:49.148
to The Slow Mo Guys
right now,

00:05:49.181 --> 00:05:50.483
for our latest videos.

00:05:50.516 --> 00:05:51.717
Yes, stay connected
with us

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:53.953
so we can stay
connected with you.

00:05:53.986 --> 00:05:55.454
- Creepy.
- Sorry.

00:05:55.487 --> 00:05:56.989
- A bit creepy.
- Sorry.

